{
  "about": "Den Web's contract with den-atlas's /index/filter routes: each url, and the canonical url atlas answers it as (the Content-Location it names when they differ). A client that always builds the canonical form shares one cache entry per question. The type is movie, series or all (both); under all a like names its title's type, like:movie-550 or like:series-1396, and a bare id is refused. people.json and people/counts.json take the person traits as `traits`, written as `sel` is and placed after it; `birthcountry` is an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code, uppercased, or a Q-id, each canonical as itself; `born` is a decade (born:1970) or one range of birth years, ends inclusive and either left out (born:1976-1996, born:1976-, born:-1996), with no other positive born pick beside it. people.json's `order` follows `traits`, lowercased, and is left out when it is the default, `prominence`. people/values/<trait>.json (gender, citizenship, occupation, birthplace, birthcountry) takes sel, traits, q and limit, in that order, as values/<kind>.json does. An item may OR values of its kind with a literal `|` (country:FR|IT; %7C is a second spelling): its ids sorted as strings and each kept once, the item sorted among the others by its ids joined with `|`, a one-value group written without `|`; a group counts toward the 16-value cap by its values; like and a born range never go in a group. `refused` are answered 400. Checked by den-atlas's filter::tests::the_canonical_fixture_holds.",
